    "stem": "According to Paragraph 4, the stress women confront tends to be _______.",
    "stemTranslation": null,
    "options": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "domestic and temporary.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "CONTRADICTION",
        "analysis": "反向混淆。第4段第5句确实提到了家庭环境（domestic situations），但后半句立刻强调 'tend not to be one-shot deals' 且在 S2 中指出是 'chronic or repeated'，这表明该压力是长期持续的，绝非暂时的（temporary 与 chronic 语义直接相悖）。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "domestic",
            "ipa": "[dəˈmestɪk]",
            "meaning": "家庭的",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          },
          {
            "word": "temporary",
            "ipa": "[ˈtemprəri]",
            "meaning": "暂时的",
            "level": "red",
            "isSelfAnnotated": true
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": true
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "irregular and violent.",
        "isCorrect": false,
        "distractorType": "ATTRIBUTION_ERROR",
        "analysis": "张冠李戴。第4句明确指出遭遇偶发随机暴力（random physical violence）的是‘男性（Men are exposed to...）’，选项将男性的压力特征硬套在女性身上。",
        "vocab": [
          {
            "word": "violent",
            "ipa": "[ˈvaɪələnt]",
            "meaning": "暴力的",
            "level": "green",
            "isSelfAnnotated": false
          }
        ],
        "selfAnnotated": false
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "durable and frequent.",
        "isCorrect": true,
        "distractorType": null,
        "analysis": "正确选项。第4段精准定位：耶胡达在S2指出女性面对的生活事件 'tend to be in more of a chronic or repeated nature'（往往具有更多长期性或反复性的性质），并在S5再次确认 'they tend not to be one-shot deals'（它们往往不是一次性的了结）。chronic（慢性的/长期的）与 durable（持久的/耐用的）完美呼应；repeated（反复的/重现的）与 frequent（频繁的/经常的）精准对应，选项 C 是对原句最高规格的同义改写。",
